ult properties:map[calculated_time:map[description:The calculated time in RFC3339 format example:2024-01-15T10:30:00+08:00 type:string]] type:object]] map[description:Tool for executing local bash (Linux/Mac) or cmd (Windows) commands. Use this tool when user needs to run system commands, check system status, or perform local operations. Returns command output, error messages, and exit code. 当用户需要执行系统命令、根据软件运行的系统类型，选择对应的系统命令。使用这个工具时，务必确保输入的命令是安全的，并且不会对系统造成破坏。系统的类型是:windows name:execute_command parameters:map[properties:map[command:map[description:The command to execute type:string]] required:[command] type:object] results:map[description:Execution results of the command including output, error messages, and exit code properties:map[command:map[description:The command that was executed example:ls -la type:string] error:map[description:Error message if the command failed (only present if there was an error) example:exit status 127 type:string] exit_code:map[description:Exit code of the command (only present if the command failed) example:%!s(int=127) type:integer] output:map[description:Standard output and error from the command example:total 24
drwxr-xr-x 5 user group 4096 Jan 15 10:30 . type:string] success:map[description:Whether the command executed successfully example:%!s(bool=true) type:boolean]] type:object]] map[description:
	Writes a chunk of content to a file at a specific offset.
	
	This tool is designed for writing large files that exceed the token limit.
	You should break down large content into smaller chunks and call this tool
	multiple times, each with a different offset.
	
	IMPORTANT: 
	- The first call should have offset = 0
	- Subsequent calls should have offset equal to total size of previously written content
	- The last chunk should have is_last = true
	- If is_last is true, file will be truncated at current offset + content length
	- CRITICAL: Each chunk must not exceed 100 characters to ensure reliable processing
	
	To use this tool:
	1. Provide the actual filename, content, offset, and is_last values
	2. Do NOT provide the parameter schema/definition
	3. Call this tool multiple times for large files, each time with the next offset
	
	Args (example values):
	{
	  "filename": "large_file.txt",
	  "content": "First part of the content...",
	  "offset": 0,
	  "is_last": false
	}
	
	Example usage for writing a large file:
	1. First chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "First part of the content...",
	     "offset": 0,
	     "is_last": false
	   })
	   
	2. Second chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "Second part of the content...",
	     "offset": 1024,
	     "is_last": false
	   })
	   
	3. Last chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "Last part of the content...",
	     "offset": 2048,
	     "is_last": true
	   })
	   
	Note: When writing large files, ensure each chunk is within the 100 character limit
	for reliable processing. If a chunk exceeds this limit, it may be truncated or fail.
	 name:write_file_chunk parameters:map[properties:map[content:map[description:The content chunk to write to the file. type:string] filename:map[description:The path to the file. Can be an absolute path or a relative path. type:string] is_last:map[description:True if this is the last chunk, false otherwise. type:boolean] offset:map[description:The byte offset in the file where this chunk should be written. type:integer]] required:[filename content offset is_last] type:object] results:map[description:Result of the file write operation properties:map[bytes_written:map[description:Number of bytes written in this chunk example:%!s(int=1024) type:integer] filename:map[description:The absolute path of the file that was written to example:/path/to/large_file.txt type:string] is_last:map[description:Indicates whether this was the last chunk to write example:%!s(bool=false) type:boolean] offset:map[description:The offset in the file where the chunk was written example:%!s(int=0) type:integer] success:map[description:Indicates whether the write operation was successful example:%!s(bool=true) type:boolean]] type:object]] map[description:Tool for getting the current real-time date and time from the server. MUST use this tool when user asks about current time, today's date, or any time-related questions requiring real-time information. Returns date, time, weekday, lunar date, and holiday information.只要对话里涉及时间的要应该先调用这个接口获取当前时间，再根据用户需求进行回复 name:get_current_time parameters:map[properties:map[] required:[] type:object] results:map[description:Current time information including date, weekday, lunar date, and holiday properties:map[current_time:map[description:Current date and time in format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' example:2024-01-15 10:30:45 type:string] holiday:map[description:Holiday information (only present if it's a holiday) example:春节 type:string] lunar_date:map[description:Chinese lunar calendar date example:腊月初五 type:string] weekday:map[description:Day of the week in Chinese example:星期一 type:string]] type:object]] map[description:
Query financial market data and generate structured analysis.

Use this tool when:
- The user asks about stock market, crypto, or financial markets
- The query involves price, trend, or investment conditions
- The user asks about "today market", "market situation", "price movement"

You MUST use this tool instead of general search when the question is about financial markets.

This tool provides structured insights including:
- Trend analysis
- Volatility
- Risk level
- Market sentiment

Valid symbol examples:
- Stocks: AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL, TSLA
- Crypto: BTC-USD, ETH-USD
- Indices: ^GSPC (S&P 500), ^DJI (Dow Jones)

IMPORTANT: Always provide a valid market symbol in the 'symbol' parameter.
If user doesn't specify a symbol, use a default like 'AAPL' or ask the user.

Do NOT rely on search tools for market data if this tool is available.
 name:query_market parameters:map[properties:map[symbol:map[description:Market symbol (e.g., AAPL, BTC-USD, ^GSPC) type:string]] required:[symbol] type:object] results:map[description:Structured market data analysis including price, trend, volatility, and insights properties:map[analysis:map[description:Market analysis and indicators properties:map[liquidity:map[description:Market liquidity (low, normal, high) example:normal type:string] market_sentiment:map[description:Overall market sentiment (bullish, bearish, neutral) example:bullish type:string] risk_level:map[description:Risk level (low, medium, high) example:low type:string]] type:object] insights:map[description:Key market insights and observations example:[Market is in uptrend phase Volatility is low] items:map[type:string] type:array] summary:map[description:Summary of market data properties:map[change:map[description:Price change from previous close example:%!s(float64=0.5) type:number] change_percent:map[description:Percentage change from previous close example:0.33% type:string] current_price:map[description:Current market price example:%!s(float64=150.25) type:number] open:map[description:Opening price for the current period example:%!s(float64=148.5) type:number] previous_close:map[description:Previous closing price example:%!s(float64=149.75) type:number] trend:map[description:Market trend (uptrend, downtrend, sideways) example:uptrend type:string] volatility:map[description:Volatility level (low, medium, high) example:low type:string] volume:map[description:Trading volume example:%!s(int=1000000) type:integer] volume_trend:map[description:Volume trend (stable, increasing, decreasing) example:stable type:string]] type:object] symbol:map[description:Market symbol (e.g., AAPL, BTC-USD) example:AAPL type:string] timestamp:map[description:Timestamp of the data in RFC3339 format example:2024-01-15T10:30:00Z type:string]] type:object]] map[description:Converts a location name (city, address, landmark) into latitude and longitude coordinates. Input should be a place name like 'Beijing', 'New York', or 'Eiffel Tower'. Returns the coordinates and additional location details. name:geocoding parameters:map[properties:map[location:map[description:The location name to geocode. Must use 'location' as the parameter name. Examples: 'Beijing', 'Times Square', 'Tokyo Tower' type:string]] required:[location] type:object] results:map[description:Geocoding tool to convert a location name into latitude and longitude coordinates properties:map[latitude:map[description:The latitude coordinate of the location example:39.9042 type:string] longitude:map[description:The longitude coordinate of the location example:116.4074 type:string]] type:object]]]
