	Writes a chunk of content to a file at a specific offset.
	
	This tool is designed for writing large files that exceed the token limit.
	You should break down large content into smaller chunks and call this tool
	multiple times, each with a different offset.
	
	IMPORTANT: 
	- The first call should have offset = 0
	- Subsequent calls should have offset equal to total size of previously written content
	- The last chunk should have is_last = true
	- If is_last is true, file will be truncated at current offset + content length
	- CRITICAL: Each chunk must not exceed 100 characters to ensure reliable processing
	
	To use this tool:
	1. Provide the actual filename, content, offset, and is_last values
	2. Do NOT provide the parameter schema/definition
	3. Call this tool multiple times for large files, each time with the next offset
	
	Args (example values):
	{
	  "filename": "large_file.txt",
	  "content": "First part of the content...",
	  "offset": 0,
	  "is_last": false
	}
	
	Example usage for writing a large file:
	1. First chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "First part of the content...",
	     "offset": 0,
	     "is_last": false
	   })
	   
	2. Second chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "Second part of the content...",
	     "offset": 1024,
	     "is_last": false
	   })
	   
	3. Last chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "Last part of the content...",
	     "offset": 2048,
	     "is_last": true
	   })
	   
	Note: When writing large files, ensure each chunk is within the 100 character limit
	for reliable processing. If a chunk exceeds this limit, it may be truncated or fail.
	 name:write_file_chunk parameters:map[properties:map[content:map[description:The content chunk to write to the file. type:string] filename:map[description:The path to the file. Can be an absolute path or a relative path. type:string] is_last:map[description:True if this is the last chunk, false otherwise. type:boolean] offset:map[description:The byte offset in the file where this chunk should be written. type:integer]] required:[filename content offset is_last] type:object] results:map[description:Result of the file write operation properties:map[bytes_written:map[description:Number of bytes written in this chunk example:%!s(int=1024) type:integer] filename:map[description:The absolute path of the file that was written to example:/path/to/large_file.txt type:string] is_last:map[description:Indicates whether this was the last chunk to write example:%!s(bool=false) type:boolean] offset:map[description:The offset in the file where the chunk was written example:%!s(int=0) type:integer] success:map[description:Indicates whether the write operation was successful example:%!s(bool=true) type:boolean]] type:object]] map[description:Tool for getting the current real-time date and time from the server. MUST use this tool when user asks about current time, today's date, or any time-related questions requiring real-time information. Returns date, time, weekday, lunar date, and holiday information.只要对话里涉及时间的要应该先调用这个接口获取当前时间，再根据用户需求进行回复 name:get_current_time parameters:map[properties:map[] required:[] type:object] results:map[description:Current time information including date, weekday, lunar date, and holiday properties:map[current_time:map[description:Current date and time in format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' example:2024-01-15 10:30:45 type:string] holiday:map[description:Holiday information (only present if it's a holiday) example:春节 type:string] lunar_date:map[description:Chinese lunar calendar date example:腊月初五 type:string] weekday:map[description:Day of the week in Chinese example:星期一 type:string]] type:object]]]
