esults of the command including output, error messages, and exit code properties:map[command:map[description:The command that was executed example:ls -la type:string] error:map[description:Error message if the command failed (only present if there was an error) example:exit status 127 type:string] exit_code:map[description:Exit code of the command (only present if the command failed) example:%!s(int=127) type:integer] output:map[description:Standard output and error from the command example:total 24
drwxr-xr-x 5 user group 4096 Jan 15 10:30 . type:string] success:map[description:Whether the command executed successfully example:%!s(bool=true) type:boolean]] type:object]] map[description:
	Writes a chunk of content to a file at a specific offset.
	
	This tool is designed for writing large files that exceed the token limit.
	You should break down large content into smaller chunks and call this tool
	multiple times, each with a different offset.
	
	IMPORTANT: 
	- The first call should have offset = 0
	- Subsequent calls should have offset equal to total size of previously written content
	- The last chunk should have is_last = true
	- If is_last is true, file will be truncated at current offset + content length
	- CRITICAL: Each chunk must not exceed 100 characters to ensure reliable processing
	
	To use this tool:
	1. Provide the actual filename, content, offset, and is_last values
	2. Do NOT provide the parameter schema/definition
	3. Call this tool multiple times for large files, each time with the next offset
	
	Args (example values):
	{
	  "filename": "large_file.txt",
	  "content": "First part of the content...",
	  "offset": 0,
	  "is_last": false
	}
	
	Example usage for writing a large file:
	1. First chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "First part of the content...",
	     "offset": 0,
	     "is_last": false
	   })
	   
	2. Second chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "Second part of the content...",
	     "offset": 1024,
	     "is_last": false
	   })
	   
	3. Last chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "Last part of the content...",
	     "offset": 2048,
	     "is_last": true
	   })
	   
	Note: When writing large files, ensure each chunk is within the 100 character limit
	for reliable processing. If a chunk exceeds this limit, it may be truncated or fail.
	 name:write_file_chunk parameters:map[properties:map[content:map[description:The content chunk to write to the file. type:string] filename:map[description:The path to the file. Can be an absolute path or a relative path. type:string] is_last:map[description:True if this is the last chunk, false otherwise. type:boolean] offset:map[description:The byte offset in the file where this chunk should be written. type:integer]] required:[filename content offset is_last] type:object] results:map[description:Result of the file write operation properties:map[bytes_written:map[description:Number of bytes written in this chunk example:%!s(int=1024) type:integer] filename:map[description:The absolute path of the file that was written to example:/path/to/large_file.txt type:string] is_last:map[description:Indicates whether this was the last chunk to write example:%!s(bool=false) type:boolean] offset:map[description:The offset in the file where the chunk was written example:%!s(int=0) type:integer] success:map[description:Indicates whether the write operation was successful example:%!s(bool=true) type:boolean]] type:object]]]
