imary weather condition example:Partly cloudy type:string] max_precip_prob:map[description:Maximum precipitation probability (0-100) example:%!s(int=30) type:integer] max_wind_speed:map[description:Maximum wind speed in km/h example:%!s(float64=15.5) type:number] temperature_range:map[description:Temperature range in Celsius example:15.5°C ~ 22.3°C type:string] trend:map[description:Temperature trend (warming/cooling/stable) example:warming type:string]] type:object]] type:object] type:array] forecast_days:map[description:Number of days in the forecast (1-16) example:%!s(int=3) type:integer] overall_insights:map[description:Overall weather trends and patterns for the forecast period example:[Overall temperature trend: Warming up over the forecast period Rain expected on 2 day(s) during the forecast period] items:map[type:string] type:array]] type:object]] map[description:Tool for executing local bash (Linux/Mac) or cmd (Windows) commands. Use this tool when user needs to run system commands, check system status, or perform local operations. Returns command output, error messages, and exit code. 当用户需要执行系统命令、根据软件运行的系统类型，选择对应的系统命令。使用这个工具时，务必确保输入的命令是安全的，并且不会对系统造成破坏。系统的类型是:windows name:execute_command parameters:map[properties:map[command:map[description:The command to execute type:string]] required:[command] type:object] results:map[description:Execution results of the command including output, error messages, and exit code properties:map[command:map[description:The command that was executed example:ls -la type:string] error:map[description:Error message if the command failed (only present if there was an error) example:exit status 127 type:string] exit_code:map[description:Exit code of the command (only present if the command failed) example:%!s(int=127) type:integer] output:map[description:Standard output and error from the command example:total 24
drwxr-xr-x 5 user group 4096 Jan 15 10:30 . type:string] success:map[description:Whether the command executed successfully example:%!s(bool=true) type:boolean]] type:object]] map[description:
	Writes a chunk of content to a file at a specific offset.
	
	This tool is designed for writing large files that exceed the token limit.
	You should break down large content into smaller chunks and call this tool
	multiple times, each with a different offset.
	
	IMPORTANT: 
	- The first call should have offset = 0
	- Subsequent calls should have offset equal to total size of previously written content
	- The last chunk should have is_last = true
	- If is_last is true, file will be truncated at current offset + content length
	- CRITICAL: Each chunk must not exceed 100 characters to ensure reliable processing
	
	To use this tool:
	1. Provide the actual filename, content, offset, and is_last values
	2. Do NOT provide the parameter schema/definition
	3. Call this tool multiple times for large files, each time with the next offset
	
	Args (example values):
	{
	  "filename": "large_file.txt",
	  "content": "First part of the content...",
	  "offset": 0,
	  "is_last": false
	}
	
	Example usage for writing a large file:
	1. First chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "First part of the content...",
	     "offset": 0,
	     "is_last": false
	   })
	   
	2. Second chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "Second part of the content...",
	     "offset": 1024,
	     "is_last": false
	   })
	   
	3. Last chunk:
	   write_file_chunk({
	     "filename": "large_file.txt",
	     "content": "Last part of the content...",
	     "offset": 2048,
	     "is_last": true
	   })
	   
	Note: When writing large files, ensure each chunk is within the 100 character limit
	for reliable processing. If a chunk exceeds this limit, it may be truncated or fail.
	 name:write_file_chunk parameters:map[properties:map[content:map[description:The content chunk to write to the file. type:string] filename:map[description:The path to the file. Can be an absolute path or a relative path. type:string] is_last:map[description:True if this is the last chunk, false otherwise. type:boolean] offset:map[description:The byte offset in the file where this chunk should be written. type:integer]] required:[filename content offset is_last] type:object] results:map[description:Result of the file write operation properties:map[bytes_written:map[description:Number of bytes written in this chunk example:%!s(int=1024) type:integer] filename:map[description:The absolute path of the file that was written to example:/path/to/large_file.txt type:string] is_last:map[description:Indicates whether this was the last chunk to write example:%!s(bool=false) type:boolean] offset:map[description:The offset in the file where the chunk was written example:%!s(int=0) type:integer] success:map[description:Indicates whether the write operation was successful example:%!s(bool=true) type:boolean]] type:object]] map[description:传入date获取date对应日期和时间的详细信息，只要问今天适合干什么，问今天的运势，只要关于运气，玄学等等关于气运的都要调用这个接口。
	支持星座、儒略日、干支、生肖、节气、节日、彭祖百忌、吉神(喜神/福神/财神/阳贵神/阴贵神)方位、胎神方位、冲煞、纳音、星宿、八字、五行、十神、建除十二值星、青龙名堂等十二神、黄道日及吉凶、法定节假日及调休等,about almanac name:get_date_info_about_almanac parameters:map[properties:map[date:map[description:必要参数，指定查询的日期，格式为'YYYY-MM-DD'，如'2023-01-01'，或者不指定，则默认为当前时间 type:string]] required:[date] type:object] results:map[description:Comprehensive date information including solar and lunar calendar details, zodiac, festivals, and traditional almanac data properties:map[almanac:map[description:Traditional Chinese almanac information example:甲辰年 丁丑月 戊子日 (冲马 煞南) type:string] current_time:map[description:Current date and time in format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' example:2024-01-15 10:30:45 type:string] day_gan_zhi:map[description:Gan-Zhi (Stem-Branch) representation of the day example:戊子 type:string] holiday:map[description:Holiday information (only present if it's a holiday) example:春节 type:string] lunar_date:map[description:Lunar calendar date in Chinese format example:甲辰年腊月初五 type:string] month_gan_zhi:map[description:Gan-Zhi (Stem-Branch) representation of the month example:丁丑 type:string] solar_term:map[description:Solar term information (if applicable) example:小寒 type:string] weekday:map[description:Day of the week in Chinese example:星期一 type:string] year_gan_zhi:map[description:Gan-Zhi (Stem-Branch) representation of the year example:甲辰 type:string] zodiac:map[description:Chinese zodiac animal for the year example:龙 type:string]] type:object]] map[description:Calculates time by adding or subtracting duration from current time. Args format: 'operation:duration' where operation is 'add' or 'subtract', and duration is like '1h30m' (hours and minutes) name:calculate_time parameters:map[properties:map[duration:map[description:The duration to add or subtract, e.g., '1h30m' for 1 hour and 30 minutes type:string] operation:map[description:The operation to perform: 'add' or 'subtract' type:string]] required:[operation duration] type:object] results:map[description:Calculated time result properties:map[calculated_time:map[description:The calculated time in RFC3339 format example:2024-01-15T10:30:00+08:00 type:string]] type:object]] map[description:Write or update the user's in-app memo / diary file (Markdown). Same storage as the 备忘录 panel (data/memo.md).
Use for travel plans, todos, notes the user asked to keep. Prefer structured Markdown (headings, lists).
For the sidebar calendar "memo dot", include a date like YYYY-MM-DD in section_title or in the first lines of content (or use default append heading which includes the date).
mode "append" adds a new dated section; "replace" overwrites the whole memo (use only when the user explicitly wants to clear or replace everything).
Args JSON: {"content": "...", "mode": "append"|"replace", "section_title": "optional heading for append"} name:memo_write parameters:map[properties:map[content:map[description:Markdown text to save. type:string] mode:map[description:append (default): add a section; replace: overwrite entire memo. enum:[append replace] type:string] section_title:map[description:Optional section heading when mode is append; default is local date-time. type:string]] required:[content] type:object] results:map[description:Confirmation with memo file path. type:string]] map[description:Tool for getting the current real-time date and time from the server. MUST use this tool when user asks about current time, today's date, or any time-related questions requiring real-time information. Returns date, time, weekday, lunar date, and holiday information.只要对话里涉及时间的要应该先调用这个接口获取当前时间，再根据用户需求进行回复 name:get_current_time parameters:map[properties:map[] required:[] type:object] results:map[description:Current time information including date, weekday, lunar date, and holiday properties:map[current_time:map[description:Current date and time in format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' example:2024-01-15 10:30:45 type:string] holiday:map[description:Holiday information (only present if it's a holiday) example:春节 type:string] lunar_date:map[description:Chinese lunar calendar date example:腊月初五 type:string] weekday:map[description:Day of the week in Chinese example:星期一 type:string]] type:object]]]
